  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1255 AM MDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nTuesday and Wednesday, moist southwest flow will return to the area, \nbringing more showers and thunderstorms each afternoon. Best chances \nfor heavy rainfall will be over our southern mountains, as well as \nthe New Mexico border, though the entire CWA will have a chance to \nsee at least scattered precipitation. \n\nModels are still showing a lot of variability for later this week \nand into the weekend. General consensus is for upper ridging to \ncontinue building in overhead, with south to southwest flow over \nour area. That being said, some models send some shortwave \ndisturbances through while others show more steady flow. Scattered \nPOPs will remain across the region, with higher chances for heavy \nrainfall over the mountains again. This unsettled pattern will \npersist until the weekend, with some drier westerly flow moving in.\n\nTemperatures will remain near or just below seasonal levels through \nthe rest of the week, with a slight warming trend expected to set in \nthis weekend.",
